# What is DCL?

**DCL (Data Control Language)** is used to **control access and permissions** on database objects.

It defines **who can access the database and what operations they can perform.**

---

# DCL Commands

| Command | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| GRANT | Gives permissions to a user |
| REVOKE | Removes permissions from a user |

---

# 1. GRANT

The **GRANT** command is used to provide privileges to a user.

## Syntax

```sql
GRANT privilege_name
ON table_name
TO user_name;
```

---

## Grant SELECT Permission

```sql
GRANT SELECT
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

The user can only read data.

---

## Grant INSERT Permission

```sql
GRANT INSERT
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

The user can insert records.

---

## Grant UPDATE Permission

```sql
GRANT UPDATE
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

The user can update records.

---

## Grant DELETE Permission

```sql
GRANT DELETE
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

The user can delete records.

---

## Grant Multiple Permissions

```sql
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## Grant All Permissions

```sql
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## Grant All Privileges on Database

```sql
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES
ON StudentDB.*
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

# 2. REVOKE

The **REVOKE** command removes permissions from a user.

## Syntax

```sql
REVOKE privilege_name
ON table_name
FROM user_name;
```

---

## Revoke SELECT Permission

```sql
REVOKE SELECT
ON Student
FROM 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## Revoke INSERT Permission

```sql
REVOKE INSERT
ON Student
FROM 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## Revoke UPDATE Permission

```sql
REVOKE UPDATE
ON Student
FROM 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## Revoke DELETE Permission

```sql
REVOKE DELETE
ON Student
FROM 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## Revoke Multiple Permissions

```sql
REVOKE SELECT, INSERT
ON Student
FROM 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## Revoke All Permissions

```sql
REVOKE ALL PRIVILEGES
ON Student
FROM 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

# Show User Privileges

```sql
SHOW GRANTS FOR 'john'@'localhost';
```

Displays all permissions assigned to the user.

---

# Create User

```sql
CREATE USER 'john'@'localhost'
IDENTIFIED BY 'Password@123';
```

---

# Drop User

```sql
DROP USER 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

# Flush Privileges

```sql
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
```

Reloads the privilege tables.

---

# Common Privileges

| Privilege | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| SELECT | Read data |
| INSERT | Insert records |
| UPDATE | Modify records |
| DELETE | Delete records |
| CREATE | Create database objects |
| DROP | Delete database objects |
| ALTER | Modify table structure |
| INDEX | Create indexes |
| REFERENCES | Create foreign keys |
| ALL PRIVILEGES | All permissions |

