# Interview Questions

## 1. What is DCL?

DCL (Data Control Language) is used to manage user permissions and access to database objects.

---

## 2. Which commands are part of DCL?

- GRANT
- REVOKE

---

## 3. Difference between GRANT and REVOKE

| GRANT | REVOKE |
|--------|---------|
| Gives permissions | Removes permissions |

---

## 4. Give SELECT permission to a user.

```sql
GRANT SELECT
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## 5. Remove UPDATE permission from a user.

```sql
REVOKE UPDATE
ON Student
FROM 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## 6. Grant all privileges on Student table.

```sql
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES
ON Student
TO 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## 7. Display all permissions of a user.

```sql
SHOW GRANTS FOR 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## 8. Create a new user.

```sql
CREATE USER 'john'@'localhost'
IDENTIFIED BY 'Password@123';
```

---

## 9. Delete a user.

```sql
DROP USER 'john'@'localhost';
```

---

## 10. Reload privilege tables.

```sql
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
```

